  '3-day-jim-corbett-national-park-tour': {
    averageRating: 4.13,
    totalReviews: 6,
    guideRating: 4.13,
    valueRating: 4.13,
    reviews: [
      { author: "Tom", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-10", text: "It was good Driver Manish was very good Good driving, nice person, and knew his way around the attractions I had a great time", photos: ["https://images.asiabylocals.com/asiabylocals/reviews/3-day-jim-corbett-national-park-tour/6594732/1600.webp", "https://images.asiabylocals.com/asiabylocals/reviews/3-day-jim-corbett-national-park-tour/6594733/1600.webp"] },
      { author: "Jonathan", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 4, date: "2025-10-18", text: "The booking arrangements were very good and well informed through the app 4* as booked options could be clearer Travel to/from 3* as although the driver was excellent, friendly and very helpful, the car was uncomfortable, noisy and cramped, not being suitable for a 5 hour trip each way on Indian roads. Safari tours were amazing and exceeded our expectations 5*, we didn’t see any tigers or elephants but the experience was wonderful with friendly and knowledgeable guides and drivers. The Hotel 4* was good, clean, comfortable and relaxing, but limited food menu and no views,", photos: ["https://images.asiabylocals.com/asiabylocals/reviews/3-day-jim-corbett-national-park-tour/4276699/1600.webp"] },
      { author: "Howard", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-04", text: "We booked our trip months ahead and had multiple changes overtime. Taj explorers were excellent to work with, communicated rapidly and were very accommodating to all our changes. Our driver, Suresh, did an outstanding job. He was always on time, polite, and reliable. He drove safely at all times. We would recommend both Taj explorers and Suresh highly for other people." },
      { author: "Jeff", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 4, date: "2026-03-10", text: "Really good but don’t expect it to be like an African safari. It is dirt mountain roads thru the forest with much fewer animals. Tigers are pretty hard to find so don’t get your hopes up. Nice place where we stayed with good food. There is a lot of driving involved: five to seven hours to or from Delphi, and the lodge was as much as an hour from the starting points of safari drives. Worth it if you see tigers of course." },
      { author: "Rainer Wolfgang", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 2, date: "2025-10-24", text: "Von Tieren keine Spur, Tiger ist wohl nur eine Legende. Zwei verlorene Tage" },
      { author: "GetYourGuide traveler", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 3, date: "2024-10-30", text: "I enjoyed the private jeep tours. Although we didn't see any tigers we saw hornbill, a jackal, all the deer types, 2 types of primates, and many bird species. You need your passport to get into the park so carry it with you. Make sure the driver has your address before you leave to your destination or you coukd spend extra time in the car. Unfortunately we got sick from the driver and I got pneumonia after that." },
    ],
  },
