  'from-jaipur-private-ranthambore-day-trip-with-tige': {
    averageRating: 2.73,
    totalReviews: 4,
    guideRating: 2.73,
    valueRating: 2.73,
    reviews: [
      { author: "Mikhail", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-26", text: "Excellent" },
      { author: "Wolfgang Matthias", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 2, date: "2026-04-15", text: "Der Fahrer war puenktlich um 9:30 im Hotel und fuhr mich korrekt und professionnell nach Ranthambore und zurueck nach Jaipur. Der Fahrer hat seine Arbeit gut gemacht. In Ranthambore musste ich 1,5 Std. warten, bis die Herrschaften, Tourguide und Jeepfahrer, kamen. Ich fand einen letzten Platz im Jeep neben einer indischen Grossfamilie. Ich zwengte mich in den Jeep, und somit wurden die letzten freien Zentimeter des Jeeps kommerziell genutzt. Ich bezahlte ca. 18.000 Rupie, 180 Euro, fuer die Tour. Eine Unverschaemtheit! Man zahlt bereits ein Vielfaches im Vergleich zu den Einheimischen und wird wie der letzte Dreck behandelt. Die Tour war lieblos und lustlos, keiner hatte richtig Lust. Die Tour dauerte 2 Stunden und 45 Minuten. Tiger wurden keine gesichtet. Ob das uehaupt moeglich ist bei dem Rattern von dem Jeep-Motor und bei dem Geschwaetz der Leute? Fuer mich war die Tour eine Verschwendung von Geld, Ressourcen und Energie. Lieber in Jaipur bleiben, da gibt es mehr zu machen!" },
      { author: "Darren", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 1, date: "2025-11-05", text: "I hate to give a bad review for anything but this was most a horrible experience. “Safari” is a strong word for most a drive through a forest. The driver from Jaipur to Ranthambore was good, the driver was very safe and overall a very good driver. However the activity: I got dropped at a hotel in Ranthambore, and from there I waited one and a half hour to be collected by a canter with no information given to me about how long i would be waiting. After waiting an hour and a half, a canter collected me which had soaking wet seats. The guide in the canter gave little to know information about anything and the only wildlife to be seen was some peacocks, wild bore and some monkeys." },
      { author: "GetYourGuide traveler", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 1, date: "2025-10-06", text: "Bad in every way. Came to Jaipur specifically for this tour - was contacted 12 hours before it started to be told we could no longer go in the Jeep we had booked and were being downgraded to a Canter but would only be refunded a fraction of the cost difference between the two. Our start time was also pushed back. It was too late to book another tour for the next day so we had to accept. When our driver arrived they were annoyed at us because they had been told a different pick up time and had been waiting an hour. Because we had been downgraded we were told we would both get window seats on the canter - this was not the case. On the tour itself we were surrounded by loud/crying young kids. We spent large periods of the tour pulled in where we could see no wildlife to allow other vehicles to pass. The guide didn’t tell us anything about what we were seeing. 3 men stood at the front the entire time blocking the view for other passengers. Very disappointing experience." },
    ],
  },
  'from-jaipur-private-ranthambore-park-trip-with-tig': {
    averageRating: 4.08,
    totalReviews: 6,
    guideRating: 4.08,
    valueRating: 4.08,
    reviews: [
      { author: "Leo", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-12-18", text: "I recently booked a Tiger Safari in Ranthambore through Raj Cabs, and it was an exceptional experience. The driver was punctual, friendly, and knowledgeable. The car was hygienic and comfortable, enhancing our journey. The safari itself was thrilling, with tiger sightings, thanks to our experienced guide. Raj Cabs provided a well-organized and memorable experience, making our trip truly enjoyable. Highly recommended!" },
      { author: "Florian", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 1, date: "2024-03-17", text: "Die eigentliche Safari war gut. Allerdings war der Weg dorthin und zurück die reinste Zumutung. Während der Fahrer noch ganz ok war, war der Guide schrecklich. Englischkenntnisse nicht vorhanden. Fahrer sehr unhygienisch, spuckte aus dem Fenster und traf uns. Darauf angesprochen, entschuldigte er sich zwar, versuchte aber such zu erklären dass Inder das so machen. Die abschließende Krönung war dann noch dass die Firma auch noch wusste, dass dieser Guide ungeeignet ist. Indischer Service ist normalerweise gut bis sehr gut, hier aber einfach nur eine Katastrophe." },
      { author: "Weronika", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 3, date: "2024-03-13", text: "Kierowca bardzo sympatyczny i pomocny. Natomiast odgórnie przydzielana jest najgorsza strefa Safari (nr 10) na której na ogromnym obszarze żyją tylko dwa tygrysy, przez co szansa na zobaczenie ich jest bardzo mała." },
    ],
  },
