  'jaipurs-artisans-trail-a-walking-tour-with-local': {
    averageRating: 2.42,
    totalReviews: 3,
    guideRating: 2.42,
    valueRating: 2.42,
    reviews: [
      { author: "Apoorva", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 1, date: "2026-08-08", text: "Very disappointing and misleading experience. We booked this specifically so our daughter could experience traditional Rajasthani art forms such as block printing, pottery, and miniature painting. However, contrary to the description, there were no hands-on workshops at all. Every station was merely a demonstration, and the artisans seemed more interested in selling their products than engaging us in the craft. Even our guide acknowledged that the description was misleading and created an expectation of hands-on workshops, whereas the actual experience was only demonstrations. The whole purpose of booking was for our daughter to participate and learn. Had we known this beforehand, we could have simply visited local shops ourselves. We are extremely disappointed and request a full refund, as the experience did not match what was advertised and the money spent feels wasted. Don't book this tour if you are looking for hands on workshop. The workshop here meant 'workshop visit' which was." },
      { author: "GetYourGuide traveler", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-25", text: "Very good experience and our guide was nice as well!!! Highly recommend" },
      { author: "Marianne", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 2, date: "2026-04-17", text: "Hemant was absolutely lovely but this is a tour which they are shuffling you around shops to buy stuff - I wouldn’t bother. It was a funny experience but the prices were extortionate and it is not a local artisan tour." },
    ],
  },
